cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AI Product Testing — the course"
message: "If you refer to this material, please cite it and link to the canonical repository. Reuse needs the author's written permission; see LICENSE."
type: software
abstract: >-
  A hands-on course on testing products that embed AI: nine modules in two
  parts, thirteen exercises with worked solutions, and a capstone. Part 1
  covers test design and running a test campaign for any product; part 2 is
  built around the Definition of Trustworthy (DoT), the acceptance gate for
  behaviour where several outputs are acceptable and exact comparison stops
  being a valid oracle.
